      "content": "i get that, but it feels like you're saying the \"critics\" are just looking at it one way while the \"historians\" have the bigger picture. isn't it more accurate to say that the economic arguments against unions are usually just excuses used by corporations to stop people from getting a fair share? like, is there actually a legitimate economic reason, or is it mostly just political?",
